IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cema-types`

-- Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK) — GOAL 3: TIME LIMITS FOR
-- PROCEEDINGS (s 146A).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1979-2.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — time limits`

-- "The period of n months beginning with" x ends on the day before the
-- corresponding date, or the last day of the month if there is none.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- s 146A(2) "Proceedings for an indictable offence shall not be commenced
-- after the end of the period of 20 years beginning with the day on which
-- the offence was committed." (3) "Proceedings for a summary offence shall
-- not be commenced after the end of the period of 3 years beginning with that
-- day but, subject to that, may be commenced at any time within 6 months from
-- the date on which sufficient evidence to warrant the proceedings came to the
-- knowledge of the prosecuting authority." Within 6 months from a date: on
-- or before the corresponding date six months later.
@ref s 146A(2)-(3)
@export The last day to commence proceedings for an offence under the customs and excise Acts under s 146A of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK): for an indictable offence, the end of the 20 years beginning with the day it was committed; for a summary offence, the earlier of the end of the 3 years beginning with that day and 6 months from the date sufficient evidence came to the prosecuting authority's knowledge. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS AN `Offence timing`  @desc The day the offence was committed, whether it is indictable, and when sufficient evidence became known
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence proceedings for` t MEANS
    IF   t's `indictable`
    THEN `the last day of the` 240 `months beginning with` (t's `committed on`)
    ELSE `the earlier of` threeYears sixMonths
    WHERE
        threeYears MEANS `the last day of the` 36 `months beginning with` (t's `committed on`)
        sixMonths MEANS `add months` (t's `sufficient evidence known on`) 6
